  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Paste-up Night",
    "overview": "RoomChat is a paste-up board worked on late: copy-paper sheets pinned and taped to a wall, a single fluorescent yellow marker, condensed poster capitals for heads and room codes, and a newspaper serif for everything you read. The main theme is the black wall (dark); light is a warm-grey board with white sheets; black is the same board in neutral grey. Every element exists in all three, and only the board and sheet stocks change.\n\nDepth comes from paper, not boxes: sheets lift off the board on soft shadows, controls sit on a hard ink offset and press into it, pinned sheets rest at small tilts. The landing page is an Evidence Board: cards on a fixed-size canvas, joined by yellow tape lines, that a visitor can drag (the tape follows). The app screens (login, register, dashboard, room) use the same sheets, pins, tape and motion, but nothing on them moves under the pointer. Under 900px a board stacks its cards in reading order with no tape and no dragging.\n\nMotion is paper physics: sheets drop onto the board as they scroll in, stamps thunk down, a new chat message drops in like a slip, a joining member's row flashes a fluorescent edge, a swapped label pops. All of it stops under `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three boards switched by `data-mode` on `<html>` (light, dark, black); with nothing stored, the OS picks light or dark.",
      "One fluorescent yellow, used as paper (a fill with toner type), never as a text colour.",
      "Square corners everywhere; only pushpins are round.",
      "League Gothic capitals for heads and codes, Newsreader for reading, Geist Mono only for technical notes, frames and data.",
      "Soft paper lifts under sheets, a hard 4px ink offset under buttons.",
      "Draggable evidence board on the landing; static boards in the app."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Fluorescent Rule",
        "body": "Fluorescent yellow fills the primary control and at most one sheet per screen, always with toner type. It is paper, never a word colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Own Paper Rule",
        "body": "Your own messages are yellow-tinted copy paper with toner ink in every theme; other people's are plain sheet paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Plain White Rule",
        "body": "The light board is warm grey with white sheets on it. White is a sheet, never the board.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Poster Caps Rule",
        "body": "League Gothic is always uppercase and only for heads, codes, stamps and big counted figures; it never sets a sentence of body text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Technical Rule",
        "body": "Geist Mono appears only for technical notes, protocol frames, data and captions. Never for headings or prose.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Caption Below Rule",
        "body": "Labels and captions go under the thing they describe (\"Fig. 2: …\"). No kicker or eyebrow line above a heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Press Into The Offset Rule",
        "body": "A button sits on a 4px ink offset, drops 1px toward it on hover, and presses fully into it on click.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Small Tilt Rule",
        "body": "Pinned sheets rest at tilts between about -1.5deg and 2.5deg; stickers and stamps may go to about 6deg. Inputs, tables and long reading stay square.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put toner type on every fluorescent, own-message and coloured-paper surface, in all three themes.",
      "**Do** keep fluorescent to the primary control and one sheet per screen.",
      "**Do** give every element a value in all three boards through the tokens; never hardcode a board colour.",
      "**Do** set captions in Geist Mono under the thing they label.",
      "**Do** keep dragging to the landing's Evidence Board; app screens are static.",
      "**Do** stop every animation under `prefers-reduced-motion`, and show revealed content at full opacity."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use plain white as the light board; white is for sheets.",
      "**Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow line above a heading.",
      "**Don't** use Geist Mono for headings or prose.",
      "**Don't** round corners; only pushpins are round.",
      "**Don't** use fluorescent yellow as a text colour on the board.",
      "**Don't** tilt inputs, tables or long reading."
    ]
  }
